cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
title: "Does a mayor improve a city beyond chance? Missing data at a change of mayor makes the test say yes: Replication package"
abstract: >-
  Replication package of the methods paper that measures, in a translation of the default path of
  the official code of the rifle package (Berry and Fowler) and on the real tenure structure of
  5,468 Brazilian municipalities (2005-2024), the size of the randomization inference test for
  leader effects when one period is missing in the middle of the series. Under modest serial
  correlation, the default gap stitching takes rejection under the null to 76.6% (gap in period 9)
  and 89.4% (gap next to a change of mayor) in the full panel; the package's own nostitch option
  removes this inflation. It carries the code, the anonymized panel, the frozen outputs with sha256,
  the tests that lock every number of the paper, the provenance chain, figures and Table 1 in four
  languages, and the paper in Portuguese (original), English, Spanish and Italian.
